1
00:00:05,638 --> 00:00:07,507
[shivering]

2
00:00:14,213 --> 00:00:17,050
Well, this certainly has been
a glorious day,

3
00:00:17,183 --> 00:00:18,551
but I'd better get back
to class.

4
00:00:18,985 --> 00:00:20,420
[mumbling]

5
00:00:20,553 --> 00:00:22,088
[chuckles]
You said it, buddy.

6
00:00:22,222 --> 00:00:24,557
Where do you think
you're going SquarePants?!

7
00:00:24,823 --> 00:00:25,758
You just got here.

8
00:00:25,892 --> 00:00:27,093
Well, I'm sorry, Sandy,

9
00:00:27,226 --> 00:00:28,193
but I just got to get back
to class.

10
00:00:28,327 --> 00:00:29,429
Sure you can't stay

11
00:00:29,562 --> 00:00:31,197
for just a short spell,
SpongeBob?

12
00:00:31,330 --> 00:00:32,598
I mean, it's such a nice day

13
00:00:32,732 --> 00:00:34,834
and everyone's having
a good time.

14
00:00:34,967 --> 00:00:36,535
[all]
Hi, SpongeBob!

15
00:00:36,669 --> 00:00:40,506
No. I gave Mrs. Puff my word
and I shall not betray her.

16
00:00:40,773 --> 00:00:43,809
Not even for a game of badminton
with me and Dale here?

17
00:00:43,943 --> 00:00:45,511
Okay, maybe just one game.

18
00:00:46,579 --> 00:00:50,015
I'm serving it up, SpongeBob,
ready or not!

19
00:00:50,883 --> 00:00:52,885
Patrick, you remember
how to play this game?

20
00:00:53,018 --> 00:00:54,386
Mm-mm.

21
00:00:55,454 --> 00:00:57,390
Is this the one
with the lowest score wins?

22
00:00:59,392 --> 00:01:01,794
Nice job, SpongeBob.
You're serve.

23
00:01:01,928 --> 00:01:03,830
Here it comes!

24
00:01:04,330 --> 00:01:07,067
[grunting]

25
00:01:08,734 --> 00:01:10,804
Hey, I'm getting pretty good
at this game.

26
00:01:18,344 --> 00:01:20,947
He's about to beat
the undefeated Sandy Cheeks

27
00:01:21,080 --> 00:01:22,514
at her own game.

28
00:01:22,748 --> 00:01:28,621
SpongeBob! SpongeBob! SpongeBob!
SpongeBob! SpongeBob! SpongeBob!

29
00:01:28,755 --> 00:01:33,993
SpongeBob! SpongeBob! SpongeBob!
SpongeBob! SpongeBob!

30
00:01:34,260 --> 00:01:37,330
[grunting]

31
00:01:40,933 --> 00:01:43,236
Yay!

32
00:01:53,212 --> 00:01:55,148
[chuckles]
Excuse me, ma'am.

33
00:01:55,281 --> 00:01:56,382
[whistling

34
00:01:56,515 --> 00:01:59,752
Hey, best friend,
check this out.

35
00:02:01,521 --> 00:02:03,356
It's a small plastic disc
that you throw.

36
00:02:03,489 --> 00:02:05,792
Small plastic disc
that you throw?!

37
00:02:06,059 --> 00:02:07,160
I love playing

38
00:02:07,293 --> 00:02:09,295
small plastic disc
that you throw.

39
00:02:09,428 --> 00:02:10,963
I do too, buddy.

40
00:02:11,097 --> 00:02:12,998
If only small plastic disc
that you throw had a shorter,

41
00:02:13,132 --> 00:02:14,033
catchier name.

42
00:02:14,166 --> 00:02:16,535
Oh. Oh! How about

43
00:02:16,669 --> 00:02:19,338
small plastic disc
that you toss?

44
00:02:19,471 --> 00:02:23,576
Perfect! Now run along, Patrick
and I'll toss it to ya!

45
00:02:24,844 --> 00:02:26,212
Ready?!

46
00:02:27,747 --> 00:02:32,919
[laughing]

47
00:02:33,052 --> 00:02:34,186
[laughing]

48
00:02:34,320 --> 00:02:35,788
That's why they
call it a sandwi...

49
00:02:35,921 --> 00:02:39,459
[laughing]

50
00:02:41,127 --> 00:02:44,464
[laughing]

51
00:02:47,366 --> 00:02:48,868
I caught it!

52
00:02:49,735 --> 00:02:51,170
Good work, man.

53
00:02:51,303 --> 00:02:52,204
[gasping]

54
00:02:52,338 --> 00:02:53,573
I see you've read my book.

55
00:02:53,739 --> 00:02:55,274
Craig Mammalton?

56
00:02:55,407 --> 00:02:57,877
The tanest man on TV?

57
00:02:59,012 --> 00:03:01,381
[chuckles]
None other.

58
00:03:03,483 --> 00:03:06,319
Oh,
look at those gorgeous wrinkles.

59
00:03:06,452 --> 00:03:08,054
What, these?

60
00:03:08,187 --> 00:03:10,656
[cheering]

61
00:03:10,789 --> 00:03:15,427
Oh, and his skin,
it's so leathery.

62
00:03:15,728 --> 00:03:18,898
Well, I don't mean to brag,
but, uh...

63
00:03:20,166 --> 00:03:23,035
[cheering]

64
00:03:23,168 --> 00:03:24,269
Whose Craig Mammalton?

65
00:03:24,703 --> 00:03:26,972
You don't know
who Craig Mammalton is?

66
00:03:27,105 --> 00:03:29,508
He's like so tan.

67
00:03:29,642 --> 00:03:32,345
Legend has it that his tan is
so deep

68
00:03:32,478 --> 00:03:37,049
that even his bones are
rich caramel brown.

69
00:03:37,183 --> 00:03:38,351
Wow.

70
00:03:38,484 --> 00:03:41,053
His mother must be so proud.

71
00:03:41,420 --> 00:03:42,955
Please, people, please,

72
00:03:43,089 --> 00:03:46,192
there'll be plenty of time
to admire my body this weekend

73
00:03:46,325 --> 00:03:48,794
at my annual summer shindig.

74
00:03:48,961 --> 00:03:53,399
[cheering]

75
00:03:55,267 --> 00:03:59,839
Wow, Patrick, an invitation
to our first summer shindig.

76
00:04:00,372 --> 00:04:01,741
And here it is.

77
00:04:03,443 --> 00:04:05,678
Can I help you, little fella?

78
00:04:06,245 --> 00:04:07,346
Seems to be stuck.

79
00:04:08,013 --> 00:04:10,783
Yeah, I don't think
this is your type of party.

80
00:04:10,917 --> 00:04:12,651
I don't want to embarrass
you guys...

81
00:04:12,785 --> 00:04:15,188
Hey, everyone, check this out!

82
00:04:16,088 --> 00:04:18,858
...but this party is
for the pigmentally gifted.

83
00:04:19,759 --> 00:04:21,593
Must be this tan to enter.

84
00:04:22,027 --> 00:04:23,963
And your skin is as light
and smooth

85
00:04:24,096 --> 00:04:25,932
as, uh, well as a baby's bottom.

86
00:04:26,065 --> 00:04:30,102
[laughing]

87
00:04:30,235 --> 00:04:31,637
Why, thank you.

88
00:04:31,770 --> 00:04:34,573
We did put on a few extra coats
of sunscreen today.

89
00:04:34,707 --> 00:04:39,312
In fact...
it's time for another coat.

90
00:04:42,347 --> 00:04:44,384
We've got to look our best.

91
00:04:45,718 --> 00:04:46,419
Losers.

92
00:04:46,552 --> 00:04:47,853
[laughing]

93
00:04:47,986 --> 00:04:50,757
You're not coming to my party...
without a tan.

94
00:04:52,525 --> 00:04:55,795
So, Squidward,
what you wanna talk about?

95
00:04:55,928 --> 00:05:00,032
Well, it's, uh, kind of hard
to put into words.

96
00:05:00,532 --> 00:05:02,301
Oh, I've been there, amigo.

97
00:05:02,434 --> 00:05:03,636
You have?

98
00:05:03,769 --> 00:05:05,738
Sure,
but nothing clears the sawdust

99
00:05:05,871 --> 00:05:08,808
out of your brains quicker
than a ride on a jet ski.

100
00:05:08,941 --> 00:05:11,044
Ever been
on one of these little babies?

101
00:05:11,277 --> 00:05:15,280
Um, no, they always seemed
a little sporty for me.

102
00:05:15,414 --> 00:05:16,882
Well, you only live once.

103
00:05:17,015 --> 00:05:20,353
And I just happen to have
an extra helmet.

104
00:05:21,287 --> 00:05:23,089
What the heck.

105
00:05:45,878 --> 00:05:46,946
Hey!

106
00:05:50,916 --> 00:05:52,352
[sighing]

107
00:05:53,252 --> 00:05:54,353
Ow!

108
00:05:54,553 --> 00:05:56,923
Ow! Hey, watch it!

109
00:06:03,629 --> 00:06:06,398
[snoring]

110
00:06:06,765 --> 00:06:08,134
There's blubber mouth.

111
00:06:08,267 --> 00:06:09,535
[snoring]

112
00:06:12,404 --> 00:06:14,507
There's Plankton's patty.

113
00:06:15,474 --> 00:06:16,409
You know what to do.

114
00:06:16,542 --> 00:06:17,777
Do I?

115
00:06:19,078 --> 00:06:20,012
Oh, yeah.

116
00:06:20,145 --> 00:06:21,947
[snoring]

117
00:06:22,147 --> 00:06:25,951
[groaning]

118
00:06:26,084 --> 00:06:28,588
[screaming]

119
00:06:29,755 --> 00:06:34,760
[groaning]
Oh, well. No patty for Plankton.

120
00:06:34,894 --> 00:06:36,795
[crying]

121
00:06:37,296 --> 00:06:38,664
I'm going in.

122
00:06:41,100 --> 00:06:43,435
Eh. Just being
near a whale's mouth

123
00:06:43,569 --> 00:06:46,105
gives me the creeps.
[screaming]

124
00:06:46,438 --> 00:06:48,807
[screaming]

125
00:06:48,941 --> 00:06:52,412
Quiet, you fool,
you'll wake up Pearl.

126
00:06:57,917 --> 00:06:58,984
[snoring]

127
00:06:59,518 --> 00:07:02,922
[sighing]
Smell that fresh seawater.

128
00:07:04,590 --> 00:07:05,557
Oh.
[chuckles]

129
00:07:05,691 --> 00:07:07,026
Right. Sorry.

130
00:07:11,063 --> 00:07:11,797
[sighing]

131
00:07:11,930 --> 00:07:13,232
[yawning]
See Sandy,

132
00:07:13,365 --> 00:07:16,769
nothing to worry about.
Baby sitting is easy.

133
00:07:17,269 --> 00:07:20,773
[snoring]

134
00:07:21,173 --> 00:07:22,875
Hey, Uncle SpongeBob.

135
00:07:23,275 --> 00:07:24,243
Eh?

136
00:07:24,376 --> 00:07:26,112
Open your eyes.

137
00:07:27,246 --> 00:07:29,182
You're just gonna love...

138
00:07:29,849 --> 00:07:31,550
our sandy surprise.

139
00:07:31,683 --> 00:07:33,485
It's our gift to you.

140
00:07:33,619 --> 00:07:35,153
Well, isn't that sweet.

141
00:07:35,287 --> 00:07:36,722
And it won't wash away.

142
00:07:36,855 --> 00:07:38,857
Cause it's made of concrete.

143
00:07:39,291 --> 00:07:40,392
[mumbling]

144
00:07:41,293 --> 00:07:44,396
Good structural integrity,
girls, but little tight.

145
00:07:44,596 --> 00:07:45,765
So sorry, Uncle.

146
00:07:45,898 --> 00:07:47,533
We made it too small.

147
00:07:47,666 --> 00:07:49,267
But we'll get you out.

148
00:07:49,401 --> 00:07:51,937
With this wrecking ball!

149
00:07:52,471 --> 00:07:54,707
A wrecking what? Owsie.

150
00:08:00,746 --> 00:08:02,014
[squawking]

151
00:08:03,415 --> 00:08:05,117
[grunting]

152
00:08:05,384 --> 00:08:08,554
Let's all go to my house
and take a little break.

153
00:08:08,687 --> 00:08:10,623
[groaning]

154
00:08:14,326 --> 00:08:15,761
On, no.

155
00:08:16,061 --> 00:08:20,132
A stomach ache at the beach?
That's no fun.

156
00:08:20,433 --> 00:08:24,203
I wish it would go away. Huh?

157
00:08:24,336 --> 00:08:27,907
Your wish is granted.
Hold out your hand.

158
00:08:29,875 --> 00:08:32,644
Wow. What is this?

159
00:08:33,011 --> 00:08:36,816
For fast relief of indigestion,
try Gush and Flush

160
00:08:36,949 --> 00:08:39,718
and wash your pain
down the drain.

161
00:08:40,185 --> 00:08:43,055
And my stupid husband
while you're at it.

162
00:08:44,256 --> 00:08:45,625
[sighing, groaning]

163
00:08:45,758 --> 00:08:47,593
[arguing]

164
00:08:47,826 --> 00:08:49,227
[screaming]

165
00:08:49,661 --> 00:08:50,963
[groaning]

166
00:08:52,097 --> 00:08:53,666
[screaming]

167
00:08:55,034 --> 00:08:58,237
Thank you extra strength
Gush and Flush.

168
00:08:58,370 --> 00:08:59,605
[chuckles]

169
00:09:01,507 --> 00:09:08,246
[grunting]

170
00:09:08,380 --> 00:09:10,016
Let's kick it up a notch.

171
00:09:12,284 --> 00:09:18,190
[grunting]

172
00:09:18,323 --> 00:09:20,092
[grunting]

173
00:09:23,462 --> 00:09:25,798
[screaming]

174
00:09:26,365 --> 00:09:29,936
[panting]

175
00:09:30,069 --> 00:09:33,439
[panting]

176
00:09:33,572 --> 00:09:38,244
[groaning]

177
00:09:39,745 --> 00:09:41,246
Shee-oot, SpongeBob.

178
00:09:41,413 --> 00:09:43,915
How we gonna go swimming
when you're in a shirt and tie?

179
00:09:44,216 --> 00:09:47,052
Oh, yes, how foolish of me.
[laughing]

180
00:09:47,186 --> 00:09:50,222
Allow me to remedy
said situation right now.

181
00:09:50,590 --> 00:09:52,024
I will just use
this changing tent here

182
00:09:52,157 --> 00:09:54,327
to change into my bathing suit.

183
00:09:55,461 --> 00:09:56,862
And I won't do anything else.

184
00:09:57,396 --> 00:09:58,630
SpongeBob's acting jumpier

185
00:09:58,764 --> 00:10:00,599
than a rattlesnake
in a pickle barrel.

186
00:10:00,866 --> 00:10:02,368
Wait. What?

187
00:10:02,501 --> 00:10:04,035
[laughing]

188
00:10:04,169 --> 00:10:08,040
Oh, I'll be changing, all right,
but not into a bathing suit.

189
00:10:08,240 --> 00:10:11,877
Wait until Sandy sees
that I brought my karate gear.

190
00:10:12,010 --> 00:10:16,882
Hi-yah! Hi-yah!
Sandy won't beat me this time

191
00:10:17,016 --> 00:10:19,185
because I've got
the elements on my side,

192
00:10:19,318 --> 00:10:23,188
the elements of surprise.
Hi-yah!

193
00:10:23,989 --> 00:10:25,657
[Sandy]
SpongeBob! Are you ready?

194
00:10:25,791 --> 00:10:29,227
Yeah, Sandy,
I most certainly am ready.

195
00:10:29,628 --> 00:10:31,363
Ready to get it on.

196
00:10:31,730 --> 00:10:34,600
- Hi-i-i...
- Hi-yah!

197
00:10:34,767 --> 00:10:38,070
Look, SpongeBob,
we both brought our karate gear.

198
00:10:38,237 --> 00:10:39,138
[laughing]

199
00:10:39,271 --> 00:10:41,406
Great minds think alike,
I suppose.

200
00:10:41,540 --> 00:10:43,009
Hi-yah!

201
00:10:49,181 --> 00:10:51,684
I may be down, but I'm not out.

202
00:10:53,385 --> 00:10:54,787
Way to go, buddy.

203
00:10:54,920 --> 00:10:57,122
It took us three days
to make that potato salad.

204
00:10:57,389 --> 00:10:59,025
Three days!

205
00:10:59,225 --> 00:11:01,894
Hi-yah! Sandy?

206
00:11:02,027 --> 00:11:08,200
Oh, I'm Sandy, all right.
I'm very sandy. Hi-yah!

207
00:11:08,333 --> 00:11:11,804
Oh, I get it.
She's Sandy.

208
00:11:11,937 --> 00:11:15,074
That's her name
and she's also covered in- yes.

209
00:11:16,775 --> 00:11:20,012
On your mark, get set, eat!

210
00:11:28,120 --> 00:11:31,456
Wow, you two are off
like a herd of turtles.

211
00:11:31,756 --> 00:11:32,992
Watch this.

212
00:11:37,429 --> 00:11:38,998
[grunting]

213
00:11:49,708 --> 00:11:51,977
[belching]
I win.

214
00:11:58,517 --> 00:11:59,851
Hot dang!

215
00:11:59,985 --> 00:12:01,887
I'm faster than green grass
through a goose.

216
00:12:02,021 --> 00:12:04,923
Hmm. These jumbo dogs are
much too big

217
00:12:05,057 --> 00:12:06,559
for your baby heads.

218
00:12:06,692 --> 00:12:08,994
[grunting]

219
00:12:09,128 --> 00:12:12,098
These dinky dogs should do ya.

220
00:12:14,233 --> 00:12:15,534
Thank you.

221
00:12:15,700 --> 00:12:16,936
You're welcome!

222
00:12:17,136 --> 00:12:18,471
[air horn sounding]

223
00:12:25,277 --> 00:12:26,746
Ee-yah!

224
00:12:28,881 --> 00:12:32,785
I win again! That's right.

225
00:12:32,918 --> 00:12:34,820
[groaning]

226
00:12:34,953 --> 00:12:38,791
I own all of y'all. Yeehaw!

227
00:12:38,924 --> 00:12:40,459
What a beautiful day.

228
00:12:40,592 --> 00:12:42,527
You said it, pal.

229
00:12:42,661 --> 00:12:44,630
Can you believe that sun?

230
00:12:44,763 --> 00:12:47,266
I could look at it all day.

231
00:12:47,833 --> 00:12:49,201
Huh? Patrick?

232
00:12:50,836 --> 00:12:52,670
- What?
- Nothing.

233
00:12:52,804 --> 00:12:54,907
So, how's that tan coming?

234
00:12:55,040 --> 00:12:57,076
I don't know. Let me check.

235
00:12:57,943 --> 00:12:59,444
Looking good.

236
00:12:59,844 --> 00:13:00,879
How's yours?

237
00:13:01,012 --> 00:13:03,949
Just a minute.
[screaming]

238
00:13:06,118 --> 00:13:08,654
I could have sworn
I was laying on my back.

239
00:13:08,854 --> 00:13:12,391
[laughing]

240
00:13:12,691 --> 00:13:13,625
Yeah!

241
00:13:13,758 --> 00:13:15,094
Whoo!

242
00:13:16,661 --> 00:13:20,032
Larry! Larry! Larry! Larry!

243
00:13:20,165 --> 00:13:23,936
Hey, it's Larry the life guard.

244
00:13:24,069 --> 00:13:26,571
Mr. Lifeguard,
can I feel your muscle?

245
00:13:26,705 --> 00:13:29,107
Sure. Don't scratch the paint.

246
00:13:29,307 --> 00:13:31,810
Lifeguard, how's the tubage?

247
00:13:31,944 --> 00:13:33,545
Gnarly, dudes.

248
00:13:33,679 --> 00:13:36,515
Alright! Yeah! Whoo hoo!

249
00:13:36,649 --> 00:13:39,885
Lifeguard,
can you point out the snack bar?

250
00:13:40,018 --> 00:13:41,553
Right over there.

251
00:13:41,687 --> 00:13:43,989
But you guys are way too old
and unsightly for my beach.

252
00:13:44,123 --> 00:13:46,324
And I'm afraid I'm gonna have
to ask you to leave.

253
00:13:46,758 --> 00:13:47,959
So polite.

254
00:13:48,093 --> 00:13:50,395
Just like we raised him.

255
00:13:50,795 --> 00:13:51,963
What a guy.

256
00:13:52,230 --> 00:13:54,333
Is it any wonder
he's so popular?

257
00:13:54,633 --> 00:13:59,104
Just imagine...
if I were a lifeguard.

258
00:14:04,276 --> 00:14:06,912
That would be so cool.

259
00:14:07,078 --> 00:14:09,748
Oh, what do you want
to be a lifeguard for?

260
00:14:10,048 --> 00:14:14,519
Nobody really likes those guys.
Being a lifeguard is so dumb.

261
00:14:14,720 --> 00:14:18,457
All they do is blow, blow, blow
on their stupid whistles,

262
00:14:18,624 --> 00:14:21,894
rub, rub, rub that white stuff
on their noses

263
00:14:22,127 --> 00:14:26,632
and show off
their gross misshapen bodies!

264
00:14:27,266 --> 00:14:31,103
Dude, put that thing away.
They're, like, children here.

265
00:14:35,206 --> 00:14:37,108
I'm going to the snack bar.

266
00:14:37,409 --> 00:14:41,046
Who needs to be a lifeguard?
I'm cool.

267
00:14:43,982 --> 00:14:45,751
I'm every bit as cool as Larry.

268
00:14:46,051 --> 00:14:48,520
And if I'm not, let me be struck
by...

269
00:14:48,653 --> 00:14:50,588
[thundering]

270
00:14:50,722 --> 00:14:53,125
a flying ice cream truck.

271
00:14:55,026 --> 00:14:56,395
And live!

272
00:14:59,565 --> 00:15:03,869
Please do not land flying
ice cream trucks on the bathers!

273
00:15:04,002 --> 00:15:05,537
[groaning]

274
00:15:06,905 --> 00:15:08,574
SpongeBob, you okay?

275
00:15:09,408 --> 00:15:13,478
Hey, I didn't know
you were a lifeguard.

276
00:15:13,712 --> 00:15:14,613
Lifeguard?

277
00:15:14,746 --> 00:15:16,048
The nose.

278
00:15:16,749 --> 00:15:18,550
[gasping]
White stuff.

279
00:15:18,884 --> 00:15:20,286
You think I'm a lifeguard?

280
00:15:20,586 --> 00:15:23,989
Sure. There's no hiding
the lifeguard look, SpongeBob,

281
00:15:24,122 --> 00:15:25,123
and you've got it.

282
00:15:25,257 --> 00:15:26,758
You really think so?

283
00:15:26,892 --> 00:15:28,193
You bet I do.

284
00:15:28,326 --> 00:15:30,496
Say we're a little shorthanded
around here.

285
00:15:30,729 --> 00:15:32,364
How would you like to work
the beach?

286
00:15:32,497 --> 00:15:33,965
I'd love it!

287
00:15:34,533 --> 00:15:38,236
Alright.
Leave that on the bench, Kahuna.

288
00:15:38,370 --> 00:15:39,971
Hey, Annette, come here!

289
00:15:40,105 --> 00:15:42,407
I want you to meet my buddy,
SpongeBob.

290
00:15:42,741 --> 00:15:44,009
Hi.

291
00:15:44,943 --> 00:15:47,112
Babe, guy's a lifeguard.

292
00:15:47,879 --> 00:15:49,181
[whistling]

293
00:15:50,081 --> 00:15:51,016
It works!

294
00:15:51,149 --> 00:15:58,056
[music playing]

295
00:15:58,189 --> 00:16:05,063
[music playing]

296
00:16:05,196 --> 00:16:12,070
[music playing]

297
00:16:12,203 --> 00:16:19,077
[music playing]

298
00:16:19,210 --> 00:16:26,118
[music playing]

299
00:16:26,251 --> 00:16:28,520
[music playing]

300
00:16:29,020 --> 00:16:30,723
Surf's up in the Goo Lagoon.

301
00:16:35,227 --> 00:16:38,163
And here comes Larry doing
his trademark lay back.

302
00:16:39,998 --> 00:16:43,435
There goes Sandy hanging ten,
fingers, that is.

303
00:16:44,503 --> 00:16:48,574
There goes SpongeBob...
ripping his pants again.

304
00:16:56,448 --> 00:17:00,185
Hey, look, a cardboard box
washed up on the beach.

305
00:17:02,353 --> 00:17:05,491
Holy fish paste! It's a guy!

306
00:17:11,162 --> 00:17:18,070
Why?! Why?! Why?!!

307
00:17:18,637 --> 00:17:20,239
SpongeBob.

308
00:17:20,939 --> 00:17:22,608
Come closer.

309
00:17:23,775 --> 00:17:27,646
I need... I need...
[gasping]

310
00:17:27,779 --> 00:17:29,214
What do you need?

311
00:17:32,083 --> 00:17:33,719
A tailor.

312
00:17:34,920 --> 00:17:36,955
Because I ripped my pants!

313
00:17:37,088 --> 00:17:38,624
[laughing]

314
00:17:38,924 --> 00:17:40,091
[groaning]

315
00:17:40,225 --> 00:17:41,926
That kinda stuff is
uncalled for.

316
00:17:42,227 --> 00:17:43,662
What is that?

317
00:17:45,664 --> 00:17:49,134
That wasn't funny, SpongeBob.
Y'all had me worried sick.

318
00:17:53,805 --> 00:17:55,174
Dude.

319
00:17:55,907 --> 00:17:58,543
[crying]

320
00:17:58,676 --> 00:18:00,979
Plankton,
what are you doing here?

321
00:18:01,113 --> 00:18:02,948
And why are you crying?

322
00:18:03,081 --> 00:18:04,649
Oh, hi, SpongeBob

323
00:18:04,783 --> 00:18:05,884
[blowing nose]

324
00:18:06,218 --> 00:18:11,824
I'm crying because I've got
these two ice cream cones,

325
00:18:12,824 --> 00:18:14,726
but I only need one.

326
00:18:14,860 --> 00:18:17,196
[crying]

327
00:18:17,329 --> 00:18:19,498
I don't know what to do
with the other one.

328
00:18:19,898 --> 00:18:26,905
[crying]

329
00:18:27,038 --> 00:18:28,040
I'll eat one

330
00:18:28,173 --> 00:18:29,340
of those ice cream cones
for you.

331
00:18:29,774 --> 00:18:33,845
SpongeBob,
would you do that for me?

332
00:18:33,978 --> 00:18:35,347
Sure.

333
00:18:37,983 --> 00:18:39,284
SpongeBob?

334
00:18:41,186 --> 00:18:42,521
SpongeBob.

335
00:18:46,925 --> 00:18:48,760
- SpongeBob!
- Yeah?

336
00:18:49,728 --> 00:18:52,430
Isn't it great to get the things
you desire?

337
00:18:52,864 --> 00:18:55,600
Like that ice cream cone,
for instance?

338
00:18:56,501 --> 00:19:00,539
You can have anything you want
with a little training.

339
00:19:01,807 --> 00:19:02,941
Training?
- Yes.

340
00:19:03,075 --> 00:19:05,877
You just have to learn
to be more assertive,

341
00:19:06,011 --> 00:19:07,880
and I can show you how.

342
00:19:10,448 --> 00:19:12,885
- Assertive, huh?
- That's right.

343
00:19:15,286 --> 00:19:16,522
Anything I want?

344
00:19:20,292 --> 00:19:21,894
Sounds great!

345
00:19:22,394 --> 00:19:23,862
Wonderful.

346
00:19:23,995 --> 00:19:29,835
[laughing]

347
00:19:29,968 --> 00:19:37,008
[laughing]

348
00:19:37,442 --> 00:19:41,613
SpongeBob.
Don't let that guy sit on you.

349
00:19:41,946 --> 00:19:46,318
Assertiveness lesson number one:
Tell him to get off!

350
00:19:46,551 --> 00:19:50,789
Um, excuse me. Sir,
you're sitting on my body,

351
00:19:50,922 --> 00:19:52,190
which is also my face.

352
00:19:52,390 --> 00:19:54,792
No, no, be assertive.

353
00:19:55,226 --> 00:19:56,495
Beep beep.

354
00:19:57,195 --> 00:19:59,198
Not insertive!

355
00:20:01,366 --> 00:20:03,535
SpongeBob,
you missed your chance.

356
00:20:03,735 --> 00:20:07,038
You've got to be aggressive
to get the things you want.

357
00:20:07,171 --> 00:20:08,307
You're too soft.

358
00:20:08,440 --> 00:20:10,509
- But I'm a s--
- Don't say it.

359
00:20:12,945 --> 00:20:15,814
There's the guy
who took your ice cream.

360
00:20:16,181 --> 00:20:17,715
Don't you want it back?

361
00:20:17,982 --> 00:20:19,017
Ice cream.

362
00:20:19,517 --> 00:20:23,021
Listen, you, my friend's got
something to say.

363
00:20:23,222 --> 00:20:25,624
What? Who said that?
Was it you?

364
00:20:25,857 --> 00:20:29,127
Tell them off, SpongeBob.
Assert yourself!

365
00:20:29,327 --> 00:20:30,995
That's my ice cream cone.

366
00:20:31,362 --> 00:20:33,831
Great. Now let him have it!

367
00:20:34,031 --> 00:20:35,066
You can have it.

368
00:20:35,199 --> 00:20:36,501
Say thanks.

369
00:20:37,168 --> 00:20:41,239
No! I show you how.

370
00:20:41,639 --> 00:20:46,545
Hey, pencil neck.
Yeah, you. Slither over here!

371
00:20:47,012 --> 00:20:51,816
Surrender that ice cream cone
or every waking moment for you

372
00:20:51,950 --> 00:20:56,321
will become a swirling torrent
of pain and misery!

373
00:20:57,922 --> 00:20:59,357
[crying]

374
00:20:59,491 --> 00:21:01,893
Hey, that guy was crying.

375
00:21:02,027 --> 00:21:04,162
Those were tears of joy.

376
00:21:04,363 --> 00:21:06,832
He was happy
that you were assertive.

377
00:21:07,331 --> 00:21:08,833
Yeah.

378
00:21:08,967 --> 00:21:12,537
You see how wonderful life
can be... when you're maniacal?

379
00:21:12,971 --> 00:21:15,040
Uh, I thought
it was called assertive.

380
00:21:15,173 --> 00:21:16,507
Whatever.

381
00:21:16,674 --> 00:21:19,945
Well, if it got me
this ice cream, then I like it.

382
00:21:27,185 --> 00:21:28,720
Ahoy, there!

383
00:21:28,853 --> 00:21:29,587
Whoa.

384
00:21:29,721 --> 00:21:31,556
My name is Eugene Krabs,

385
00:21:31,790 --> 00:21:33,558
and I would like to know
if I can interest

386
00:21:33,691 --> 00:21:36,928
either one of you in a fresh,
delicious Krabby Patty

387
00:21:37,062 --> 00:21:38,096
fresh off the grill.

388
00:21:38,230 --> 00:21:39,197
Are they free?

389
00:21:39,330 --> 00:21:42,967
Yes. Today they're only $3 each.

390
00:21:43,101 --> 00:21:44,269
Sounds great.

391
00:21:44,403 --> 00:21:46,337
But I left my wallet
up on the sand.

392
00:21:46,470 --> 00:21:47,572
I told you.

393
00:21:47,706 --> 00:21:54,145
- Yee-ee-ee-haw!
- What?

394
00:21:54,278 --> 00:21:55,680
I love the beach.

395
00:21:55,814 --> 00:21:58,082
Oh, that noise was Sandy.

396
00:21:58,215 --> 00:22:01,720
Y'all be careful. Looks like
some big waves a comin'.

397
00:22:01,853 --> 00:22:03,988
- Who are you?
- Hey, either you buy a patty

398
00:22:04,122 --> 00:22:05,424
or get off me wave.

399
00:22:05,557 --> 00:22:06,925
Cowabunga!

400
00:22:08,259 --> 00:22:09,694
What next?

401
00:22:10,061 --> 00:22:13,631
[babbling]
Oh.

402
00:22:13,931 --> 00:22:15,199
Aloha, Patrick!

403
00:22:15,333 --> 00:22:16,567
Hey, there, young feller!

404
00:22:16,701 --> 00:22:18,236
How'd you like to be
our first customer

405
00:22:18,370 --> 00:22:20,739
in over 17 working days?

406
00:22:20,872 --> 00:22:21,773
I'd love to!

407
00:22:21,906 --> 00:22:23,708
Squidward, show him a menu.

408
00:22:24,409 --> 00:22:27,646
Uh, I can't quite see it
from here.

409
00:22:27,879 --> 00:22:29,814
I'll just have to climb
on board.

410
00:22:29,948 --> 00:22:32,784
[laughing]
That's a good one, Patrick,

411
00:22:32,917 --> 00:22:35,687
on board! Whoa! Whoa! Whoa!

412
00:22:35,820 --> 00:22:37,989
Careful!
You're gonna capsize us!

413
00:22:38,122 --> 00:22:39,424
Almost up.

414
00:22:39,557 --> 00:22:40,926
[screaming]

415
00:22:41,059 --> 00:22:42,027
You idiot!

416
00:22:42,160 --> 00:22:48,299
[groaning]

417
00:22:48,432 --> 00:22:50,402
Patrick, look out!

418
00:22:51,202 --> 00:22:52,470
Locals only!

419
00:22:52,603 --> 00:22:53,938
What'd she say?!

420
00:22:54,071 --> 00:22:57,609
[screaming]

421
00:22:58,209 --> 00:23:01,780
[screaming]

422
00:23:02,513 --> 00:23:04,883
[screaming]

423
00:23:05,016 --> 00:23:07,986
Wipe out!

424
00:23:08,419 --> 00:23:10,454
Well, if you think
you can take down this castle,

425
00:23:10,588 --> 00:23:13,024
my answer is bring it on!

426
00:23:13,157 --> 00:23:14,526
[laughing]

427
00:23:24,068 --> 00:23:24,970
[clearing throat]

428
00:23:25,437 --> 00:23:27,839
Patrick, I'm trying to be
the nice guy here, okay?

429
00:23:27,972 --> 00:23:29,607
Let's call
this silly business off.

430
00:23:29,741 --> 00:23:32,043
No way. You started it.

431
00:23:32,177 --> 00:23:34,012
Fine! Have it your way.

432
00:23:34,979 --> 00:23:36,114
[laughing]

433
00:23:36,381 --> 00:23:37,482
Whatever.

434
00:23:37,615 --> 00:23:38,884
[gasping]

435
00:23:41,485 --> 00:23:43,054
No, no, no, no.

436
00:23:44,622 --> 00:23:45,857
[screaming]

437
00:23:49,327 --> 00:23:51,897
[laughing]

438
00:23:58,302 --> 00:23:59,571
Whoa!

439
00:24:10,849 --> 00:24:13,585
Oh, hello. And goodbye.

440
00:24:13,751 --> 00:24:15,053
[screaming]

441
00:24:17,088 --> 00:24:18,223
Aha!

442
00:24:18,389 --> 00:24:20,391
[screaming]

443
00:24:20,525 --> 00:24:22,027
Come on!

444
00:24:26,431 --> 00:24:27,799
How you like them apples?

445
00:24:30,068 --> 00:24:31,102
[gasping]

446
00:24:35,306 --> 00:24:37,008
[laughing]

447
00:24:37,141 --> 00:24:40,479
You'll never win
and do ya hear me?!

448
00:24:44,715 --> 00:24:48,653
Uh-huh. Mm hmm.
Well put, General.

449
00:24:48,786 --> 00:24:51,189
We'll create
a surprise military diversion

450
00:24:51,323 --> 00:24:52,957
and break through enemy lines.

451
00:24:53,157 --> 00:24:55,727
What say you? Yes.

452
00:24:55,861 --> 00:24:57,596
We shall ready ourselves
immediately.

453
00:25:05,336 --> 00:25:07,506
How you like me now?

454
00:25:08,706 --> 00:25:10,942
I like you this much.

455
00:25:15,947 --> 00:25:16,982
Whoa!

456
00:25:18,416 --> 00:25:20,051
Feel me!

457
00:25:20,351 --> 00:25:21,953
[groaning]

458
00:25:29,560 --> 00:25:30,862
Patrick?

459
00:25:32,230 --> 00:25:34,498
Patrick! Are you okay?!

460
00:25:34,665 --> 00:25:38,169
Question is... will you be?

461
00:25:46,777 --> 00:25:50,181
[screaming]

462
00:25:51,115 --> 00:25:52,783
[laughing]

463
00:25:52,950 --> 00:25:55,120
There are lots of ways
to have fun here.

464
00:25:55,754 --> 00:25:57,722
Dudes, bury me!
[laughing]

465
00:25:57,855 --> 00:25:59,090
See what I mean?

466
00:26:00,458 --> 00:26:01,326
All done.

467
00:26:01,459 --> 00:26:03,060
All right!

468
00:26:03,194 --> 00:26:05,697
Bubble Buddy, you dig him out
while I get some cotton candy.

469
00:26:06,464 --> 00:26:09,401
Don't just stand there, dude,
the tide's coming in.

470
00:26:09,534 --> 00:26:10,936
[laughing]

471
00:26:12,770 --> 00:26:14,039
Dude?

472
00:26:19,910 --> 00:26:21,512
My friend's in there.

473
00:26:21,645 --> 00:26:23,014
Congratulations.

474
00:26:24,982 --> 00:26:29,187
Whoo! Shake it! Whoo whoo!
Shake it!

475
00:26:29,320 --> 00:26:32,958
Yeah, shake that bubble butt!
Yeah!

476
00:26:34,459 --> 00:26:36,194
[mumbling]

477
00:26:36,327 --> 00:26:37,429
Is my butt big?

478
00:26:37,562 --> 00:26:39,264
[mumbling]

479
00:26:43,267 --> 00:26:46,437
Oh, oh, oh,
it's the world-famous surfer,

480
00:26:46,570 --> 00:26:48,106
Grubby Grouper!

481
00:26:48,239 --> 00:26:49,340
Later, groupies!

482
00:26:49,473 --> 00:26:53,278
Grubby's got to go catch
some gnarly pounders.

483
00:26:53,411 --> 00:26:55,646
[howling]

484
00:26:55,813 --> 00:26:59,083
Oh, I'll never wash
this flipper again.

485
00:26:59,216 --> 00:27:02,053
Hey, Pearl,
shake hands with Bubble Buddy.

486
00:27:03,554 --> 00:27:04,789
Wha?

487
00:27:06,257 --> 00:27:09,294
[crying]

488
00:27:11,529 --> 00:27:13,464
It's his first time on his own.

489
00:27:14,031 --> 00:27:16,801
Once again, congratulations.

490
00:27:17,601 --> 00:27:19,203
Popcorn! Peanuts!

491
00:27:19,336 --> 00:27:20,805
Ice cold drinks!

492
00:27:20,938 --> 00:27:22,774
[whistling]

493
00:27:22,907 --> 00:27:27,178
Two hours is long enough!
That's it!

494
00:27:27,645 --> 00:27:30,081
Hey, Bubble Buddy,
you're finished.

495
00:27:33,984 --> 00:27:37,021
He kept us waiting for a bubble?

496
00:27:37,288 --> 00:27:40,392
That's nothing.
He called us fat.

497
00:27:42,627 --> 00:27:43,995
[crying]

498
00:27:44,128 --> 00:27:46,764
He washed my flipper.

499
00:27:47,064 --> 00:27:48,266
He owes me money!

500
00:27:48,499 --> 00:27:51,302
He made me provide
excellent service!

501
00:27:51,870 --> 00:27:54,939
Dude, he made me
experience high tide!

502
00:27:55,273 --> 00:27:58,376
Oh-h-h!

503
00:27:59,477 --> 00:28:01,012
I'm telling you, he's huge.

504
00:28:01,146 --> 00:28:02,847
Have you guys seen
SpongeBob anywhere?

505
00:28:02,980 --> 00:28:06,251
You mean MuscleBob BuffPants?
He's in there.

506
00:28:06,384 --> 00:28:08,286
Uh, whatever. Thanks.

507
00:28:09,253 --> 00:28:13,024
I start off with 20 raw eggs
every day, but that's just me.

508
00:28:13,191 --> 00:28:15,559
- Pardon me.
- Working out is my life.

509
00:28:15,726 --> 00:28:19,064
I remember when I used to look
like that guy over there.

510
00:28:19,664 --> 00:28:21,031
Who me?

511
00:28:21,465 --> 00:28:22,867
[laughing]

512
00:28:23,000 --> 00:28:25,170
I remember when
I used to look like you, too.

513
00:28:25,303 --> 00:28:26,404
[laughing]

514
00:28:26,538 --> 00:28:27,972
But that was a long time ago.

515
00:28:28,106 --> 00:28:30,075
- Here's your drink, sir.
- Thank you.

516
00:28:30,809 --> 00:28:35,480
[grunting]
Oops.

517
00:28:36,314 --> 00:28:38,283
[grunting]

518
00:28:39,750 --> 00:28:41,319
[grunting]

519
00:28:46,757 --> 00:28:48,292
[slurping]

520
00:28:48,659 --> 00:28:49,727
Yeah.

521
00:28:49,927 --> 00:28:51,295
SpongeBob?

522
00:28:52,129 --> 00:28:54,198
Wh- Where'd you get
those muscles?

523
00:28:54,332 --> 00:28:56,034
I created
my own workout routine

524
00:28:56,167 --> 00:28:57,735
that's giving me
amazing results.

525
00:28:57,869 --> 00:29:00,404
Oops. Yeah,
I have never felt better.

526
00:29:00,772 --> 00:29:02,673
- Heck, what's your secret?
- What?

527
00:29:02,807 --> 00:29:04,709
Your secret work out,
what is it?

528
00:29:04,842 --> 00:29:06,277
Yeah, I mean come on.

529
00:29:06,411 --> 00:29:07,479
Yeah, enough.

530
00:29:07,612 --> 00:29:12,617
Hmm. Well, I, uh,
first, I take my hand,

531
00:29:12,784 --> 00:29:14,352
and I do this.

532
00:29:17,354 --> 00:29:18,056
Are you kidding?

533
00:29:18,189 --> 00:29:20,225
Do these muscles lie?

534
00:29:26,130 --> 00:29:28,332
I'm glad to see you found
an exercise program

535
00:29:28,466 --> 00:29:29,433
that works for you.

536
00:29:29,567 --> 00:29:31,101
Yeah,
your workout routine wasn't

537
00:29:31,235 --> 00:29:32,603
quite tough enough for me.

538
00:29:32,770 --> 00:29:34,304
Can't argue with those results.

539
00:29:34,438 --> 00:29:37,074
What you need to do now is
put those muscles to the test.

540
00:29:37,207 --> 00:29:40,578
I don't know, SpongeBob,
this looks pretty dangerous.

541
00:29:40,711 --> 00:29:42,413
Yeah, yeah, you said it, buddy.

542
00:29:42,547 --> 00:29:45,016
Now we're really living
like Larry.

543
00:29:48,686 --> 00:29:50,321
Well, will you look at that?

544
00:29:55,693 --> 00:29:58,196
Now there's two guys
who know how to live.

545
00:29:58,963 --> 00:30:00,698
Prepare for countdown.

546
00:30:00,864 --> 00:30:02,300
I'm proud of them.

547
00:30:03,701 --> 00:30:06,704
Wait a minute,
with that angle of trajectory,

548
00:30:07,138 --> 00:30:09,673
they'll land right in...
Ripper's Reef.

549
00:30:10,240 --> 00:30:12,110
They'll be ripped to shreds!

550
00:30:13,711 --> 00:30:16,180
Wait! Don't do it! Stop!

551
00:30:16,314 --> 00:30:19,851
Three, two, one, lift off.

552
00:30:21,719 --> 00:30:23,121
Drat!

553
00:30:24,722 --> 00:30:30,228
Whoo! Whoo hoo! Whoo whoo whoo!

554
00:30:34,966 --> 00:30:36,201
Huh?

555
00:30:39,903 --> 00:30:41,873
Whoa!

556
00:30:44,041 --> 00:30:45,543
[grunting]

557
00:30:45,710 --> 00:30:48,979
Look, guys, my advice wasn't
meant to be taken literally!

558
00:30:49,180 --> 00:30:51,182
I meant to live life
to the fullest,

559
00:30:51,315 --> 00:30:54,586
not to maim yourselves!
Look!

560
00:30:55,786 --> 00:30:57,121
Uh-oh!

561
00:30:57,788 --> 00:30:59,991
[screaming]

562
00:31:00,524 --> 00:31:02,527
No!

563
00:31:05,163 --> 00:31:06,630
Well, I had better be off now.

564
00:31:06,897 --> 00:31:08,332
No!

565
00:31:08,465 --> 00:31:11,802
Don't go, SpongeBob,
think about your fans.

566
00:31:11,935 --> 00:31:13,170
Well, if it's for the fans,

567
00:31:13,304 --> 00:31:14,672
I guess I can play
just one game more.

568
00:31:14,805 --> 00:31:15,840
Not today, yellow.

569
00:31:16,073 --> 00:31:17,574
You're playing
with a convicted felon,

570
00:31:17,741 --> 00:31:20,177
and we know he's violated
his parole somehow.

571
00:31:20,310 --> 00:31:21,813
You might as well confess, Dale.

572
00:31:21,946 --> 00:31:23,981
Hey, man,
I haven't done nothing.

573
00:31:24,115 --> 00:31:26,116
Oh, yeah?
What have you got in there?

574
00:31:26,617 --> 00:31:29,286
Hmm. Quasi gummy
chewy candy fish.

575
00:31:29,720 --> 00:31:33,023
Is this how you have fun?
By eating your own kind?

576
00:31:33,157 --> 00:31:38,096
Scum like you make me sick.
Cuff him.

